TUR
# Language Alphabet
1 0 *
# Stack Alphabet
X Y A B S E
# List of states by name
# V are the (V)erification states
# F are the states used for (F)inding the least significant non-zero bit.
# S are the states used for one (S)um operation.
# SC are the states for the (S)um (C)leanup
# C are the states used for (C)leanup
# H is the (H)alt state
V0 V1 V2 V3 V4 F0 F1 F2 F3 S0 S1 S2 S2.1 S3 S3.1 S3.2 S4 SC0 SC1 SC2 SC3 C0 C1 C2 C3 C4 C4.1 C4.2 C5 C5.1 C5.2 C6 H
# List of accepting halt states, in my case I only have one.
H
# Verify the string takes the form X*Y
# If it does, this machine should always halt.
# I'm sure you could find some edge case involving spaces
# But that's above my paygrade.
V0 0 0 R V1
V0 1 1 R V1
V1 0 0 R V1
V1 1 1 R V1
V1 * * R V2
V2 0 0 R V2
V2 1 1 R V2
V2   L V3
V3 0 0 L V4
V3 1 1 L V4
V4 0 0 L V4
V4 1 1 L V4
V4 * * L F0
# Find the least significant 1 bit in the first operand.
F0 0 X R F1
F0 X X L F0
F0 1 X R S0
# If we reach the left end of the tape, then we are done multiplying
F0   R C0
# Go to the end of the tape
F1 0 0 R F1
F1 1 1 R F1
F1 * * R F1
F1 X X R F1
F1   R F2
# Confirm one bit in the eventual output.
F2 X X R F2
F2 Y Y R F2
F2  X L F3
F2 0 X L F3
F2 1 Y L F3
F3 X X L F3
F3 Y Y L F3
F3 0 0 L F3
F3 1 1 L F3
F3   L F3
# Then, we fetch another bit.
F3 * * L F0
# SUM
S0 0 0 R S0
S0 1 1 R S0
S0 X X R S0
S0 * * R S0
S0   L S1
S1 A A L S1
S1 B B L S1
S1 0 A R S2
S1 1 B R S3
S1 * * R SC0
# Add a 0
S2 A A R S2
S2 B B R S2
S2   R S2.1
S2.1 X X R S2.1
S2.1 Y Y R S2.1
S2.1 A A R S2.1
S2.1 B B R S2.1
S2.1 0 A L S4
S2.1 1 B L S4
S2.1  A L S4
# Add a 1
S3 A A R S3
S3 B B R S3
S3   R S3.1
S3.1 X X R S3.1
S3.1 Y Y R S3.1
S3.1 A A R S3.1
S3.1 B B R S3.1
S3.1 0 B L S4
S3.1 1 A R S3.2
S3.1  B L S4
# Carrying a 1
S3.2 0 1 L S4
S3.2  1 L S4
S3.2 1 0 R S3.2
# Go back to first operand of sum
S4 X X L S4
S4 Y Y L S4
S4 A A L S4
S4 B B L S4
S4 0 0 L S4
S4 1 1 L S4
S4   L S1
# SUM CLEANUP
SC0 A 0 R SC0
SC0 B 1 R SC0
SC0   R SC1
SC1 X X R SC1
SC1 Y Y R SC1
SC1 A X R SC2
SC1 B Y R SC2
SC2 A 0 R SC2
SC2 B 1 R SC2
SC2 0 0 R SC2
SC2 1 1 R SC2
SC2   L SC3
# Move the tape to before the * and go back to F
SC3 0 0 L SC3
SC3 1 1 L SC3
SC3 X X L SC3
SC3 Y Y L SC3
SC3   L SC3
SC3 * * L F0
# CLEANUP
C0 0  R C0
C0 1  R C0
C0 *  R C0
C0 X  R C0
C0  S R C1
# At C1, we have the answer in reverse, but we need to reverse and format it.
# Insert an end flag at the end of the string
C1 0 0 R C1
C1 1 1 R C1
C1 X X R C1
C1 Y Y R C1
C1  E L C2
# Go back to the start, reformatting everything along the way
C2 X 0 L C2
C2 Y 1 L C2
C2 0 0 L C2
C2 1 1 L C2
C2 S S R C3
# Copy everything in reverse.
C3   R C3
C3 0  L C4
C3 1  L C5
C3 E  L C6
# Copy 0s
C4   L C4
C4 S S L C4.1
C4.1 0 0 L C4.1
C4.1 1 1 L C4.1
C4.1  0 R C4.2
C4.2 0 0 R C4.2
C4.2 1 1 R C4.2
C4.2 S S R C3
# Copy 1s
C5   L C5
C5 S S L C5.1
C5.1 0 0 L C5.1
C5.1 1 1 L C5.1
C5.1  1 R C5.2
C5.2 0 0 R C5.2
C5.2 1 1 R C5.2
C5.2 S S R C3
# Go back, remove the start flag, and end.
C6   L C6
C6 S  L H
